+### Task 5a: A collection trigger that counts bytes
+
+**Evidence:** `.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-07-phase-6-1/whole-groups-memory.md` (section 3 and
+Recommendation 2). `Interp::collect_if_due` (`lib.rs:2637` at a46465a9f) collects only when the arena
+must grow and its slot capacity reaches `collect_at`, which starts at `COLLECT_FLOOR` = 65 536 slots. A
+300 KB string is one slot, so `do i = 1 to N; x = copies('abc', 100000); end` makes no collection in
+4000 passes and grows by about 1 GB per second; the oracle runs it in 13 MB. Earlier record:
+`docs/superpowers/records/2026-09-04-phase-5c-followup/task-1-report.md` 3.4 and `phase-4f-record.md`
+Cause A (the peak is bounded by a multiple of the live set in slots, not in bytes).
+
+**Rule (R10):** a collection is also due when the bytes held by bodies allocated since the last
+collection pass a floor or a multiple of the bytes live after it, whichever is larger; the slot test
+stays. Peak memory of a loop of dead large values is then bounded by a multiple of its live bytes.
+
+**Files:** `lib.rs` (`collect_if_due`, `collect_at`), the heap or arena module that allocates string
+and other variable-size bodies (where the byte count is kept), the collector (where live bytes are
+summed after a sweep), a corpus or crate test, `docs/superpowers/plans/phase-6-1-gate.md`.
+
+**Interfaces:** none outward. The counter is updated where a body's bytes are allocated and reset
+after a collection; byte sizes come from the body's own length, not from the allocator.
+
